{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The fourth-generation Echo Dot feels like a useful addition because voice control would complement my existing Fire TV devices.",
    "The Alexa speakers and displays fit my interest in connected-home devices, even though I only have an immediate reason to choose the Dot."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The HD Fire TV Stick adds little because I already have a 4K stick and a Fire TV television; the Cube's hands-free features are appealing but do not create a current need.",
    "The flash-drive multipack, children's tablet case, and speaker brackets require storage needs, a particular tablet, or a mounting project that my history does not indicate.",
    "The Echo Show displays are relevant to my interests, but I have no immediate use for a smart screen, video calling, or the bundled subscription trial."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My Fire TV purchases seem to have been taken as a reason to suggest more streaming devices, even when they duplicate what I already use.",
    "My electronics purchases seem to have been treated as broad interest in accessories, although usefulness depends on the specific devices and tasks involved."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "I care about what an addition lets me do beyond what my current equipment already covers; convenient voice control is more compelling now than another streaming player.",
    "Interest in Alexa does not mean I need several Alexa devices at once; choosing one speaker meets my current purpose.",
    "Accessories need a clear connection to equipment I own or a task I am trying to complete."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my connected-home interests but often confused a useful addition with more devices that repeat existing functions."
}"}
